# Vulnerabilities in the deployer image that are genuinely blocked on an
# upstream fix, not something we can patch ourselves. Any NEW finding not
# listed here still fails the scan.
#
# Google shipped a fix for the go1.26.5 stdlib CVEs on ~2026-09-21 — the
# base image's kubectl (now v1.37) and helm are built with go1.26.6/1.27.1
# respectively, confirmed clean by a full rescan. See
# https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/marketplace-k8s-app-tools/issues/688
# (still open as of this cleanup; comment there tracked it as fixed).

# Google's deployer_helm base image (13.0.17, 2026-11-09). Its kubectl
# (v1.37.2, go1.26.10) and helm (go1.27.2) binaries carry old Go modules:
# golang.org/x/net and golang.org/x/text in kubectl, x/net and the go1.27.2
# stdlib in helm. Our own nk binary is built with go1.26.10 and is not
# affected by these. Remove each entry once a rescan of a newer base image
# no longer reports it.
CVE-2026-56851
CVE-2026-78661
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-111943

# Same base image: setuptools 70.3.0 vendored with Google's deployer
# tooling. Not upgraded here to avoid changing the dependencies of Google's
# deployer scripts.
CVE-2025-47273
